  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Pocket Scrapbook",
    "overview": "Every screen is a page of coloured paper and every memory is something pasted onto it: a taped note card, a Polaroid, a folded slip. The whole app sits on a grain-textured paper ground whose colour changes by section (butter for home, blush for the journal and day page, baby blue for the gallery, sage for stats, lavender for settings and the save reward). Cream cards, Polaroid frames and pastel notes rest on that ground at slight angles, held down by washi tape. Plum ink draws everything: text, the outlines of the authored doodle stickers and mood faces, and the hand-drawn today circle.\n\nDensity is low and the tone is gentle. Most content is one column on the phone. On desktop it becomes a left rail with a two-column page. Delight comes from physical metaphors that each do a real job: the happiness jar fills with folded paper stars, the On This Day envelope breaks its seal to reveal Polaroids, and today's date gets a circle that draws itself. After dark the evening theme turns the paper deep indigo and the pastels become ink. Paper objects that are light in real life, such as Polaroids and slips, stay light.\n\nThe system rejects the habit-tracker dashboard. It has no streaks, rings, charts or KPI tiles. Numbers appear as handwritten notes (\"2/5 little happy things collected\") and never as metrics.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "A grain-textured paper ground with a different colour for each route",
      "Plum ink (#463a4f) for text and every doodle outline",
      "Three faces: Gochi Hand for headings, Yellowtail script for the wordmark, dates and quotes, and Shantell Sans for body text",
      "Washi tape strips, Polaroid frames, photo-corner mounts, and ruled or graph-paper card fills",
      "Small resting tilts (between -1.6deg and 2deg) and asymmetric \"cut paper\" corners",
      "Soft, warm, plum-tinted drop shadows; nothing glossy",
      "An evening theme that inverts the paper while light objects keep dark ink"
    ],
